s3-p14 = prose (cons "The center is \((a,\mathsf{refl}_a)\). A path \(p:a=x\) contracts \((x,p)\) to this center. Cubically, a contraction can be built using the interval connection \(i\wedge j\), so that the equality witness varies coherently with the point. This is a computational construction, not an informal appeal to uniqueness. Its dependent eliminator belongs to the same type-theoretic lineage as Martin-Löf’s identity types ([6](#ref-6))." nil)
